# UBSan runtime suppressions for the sanitize cells.
#
# Nim's stdlib codegen for the asyncdispatch event loop reads a bool field
# through the global dispatcher ref during lazy init (asyncdispatch.nim
# setGlobalDispatcher), which UBSan's `null` check reports as "load of null
# pointer of type '_Bool'". It is a benign Nim codegen artifact, not a navi
# bug, and it only reproduces on x86_64. navi cannot fix code in the Nim
# standard library, so suppress the `null` check ONLY when it originates inside
# the Nim install tree (*/nim/lib/*). navi's own sources live under /navi/src,
# never match this path, and stay fully checked (a real null-pointer load in
# navi still fails the run). Every other UBSan check stays hard-failing
# everywhere (see UBSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1 in run.sh).
null:*/nim/lib/*
